# Binary assets — declared explicitly rather than left to Git's content heuristic.
#
# This repo has core.autocrlf=true. Git normally detects binaries by looking for NUL
# bytes in the first 8KB and skips line-ending conversion for them. That heuristic is
# reliable in practice but it is a heuristic, and a webfont silently rewritten by CRLF
# conversion is corrupt in a way nothing in the build will notice — the page just
# renders in a fallback face on someone else's clone.
#
# Declaring the types removes the guess. Deliberately NOT using `* text=auto`, which
# would renormalise every tracked text file and churn the working tree.

*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.webp  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.avif  binary

*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.pdf   binary
